      "value": "@{6555d16076713d25a9a56b70|full_name} Well, I imagined that individual end users could choose the color locally if they're VRC+, so for example I could choose royal purple and that's the color I see for 18+ verified around the name plate when they speak. I don't have any real suggestion for a default color for non-VRC+ subscribers. The end goal in my mind would be displaying the color change only if you publicly have 18+ toggled for the profile. \n\nTo be honest though I suppose there's no harm in allowing for the other tiers to toggle on visibility, and then also allowing VRC+ users to customize the colors by tier.",
